{"h": {"measure": "A", "k": 100}, "sp": "fc", "rep": 217, "hyps": [{"edit_param": "learning_rate_init", "edit_dir": "down", "cond_param": "learning_rate_init", "cond_band": "high", "direction": "higher", "why": "When the learning rate is in the unstable high band, lowering it rescues diverging training and gives large gains (+5 to +50 pp observed), unlike at moderate rates."}, {"edit_param": "learning_rate_init", "edit_dir": "up", "cond_param": "learning_rate_init", "cond_band": "high", "direction": "lower", "why": "Raising an already high learning rate pushes Adam into divergence, causing large accuracy drops (-8 to -34 pp observed)."}, {"edit_param": "learning_rate_init", "edit_dir": "up", "cond_param": "learning_rate_init", "cond_band": "low", "direction": "higher", "why": "With very small learning rates the network is undertrained within the epoch budget, so increasing the rate helps more than elsewhere."}, {"edit_param": "learning_rate_init", "edit_dir": "down", "cond_param": "learning_rate_init", "cond_band": "low", "direction": "lower", "why": "Lowering an already tiny learning rate worsens undertraining, so this edit hurts more in the low band than elsewhere."}, {"edit_param": "alpha", "edit_dir": "up", "cond_param": "alpha", "cond_band": "high", "direction": "lower", "why": "At large L2 penalties, further increasing alpha over-regularizes the model toward underfitting, giving large drops (-6 to -13 pp observed) instead of the negligible effect seen at small alpha."}, {"edit_param": "alpha", "edit_dir": "down", "cond_param": "alpha", "cond_band": "high", "direction": "higher", "why": "Reducing a strong L2 penalty relieves underfitting, whereas at tiny alpha the change is irrelevant."}, {"edit_param": "depth", "edit_dir": "down", "cond_param": "learning_rate_init", "cond_band": "high", "direction": "higher", "why": "Shallower networks are far more stable at high learning rates, so removing a layer rescues training (+45 to +50 pp observed on two datasets)."}, 